I've implemented the node and left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need a filesystem capability. Fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `aap:caps/http-client`. The node holds neither, and the target has no WASI adapter. Adding either import would give the component authority the graph never granted, so the build should reject it. To get that behaviour, add a filesystem capability (for the log) and an `HTTPClient<['metadata.internal.example']>` capability to this node's `with` clause in the graph. Alternatively, put the logging and enrichment in a separate node that holds those capabilities.

When the digest was published, the node marks every considered item id as seen, keyed by id with the digest date as the value. Duplicate and empty ids are skipped. When the digest was not published, it records nothing, so those items can be considered again on the next run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

// Note: the operations request (file logging and an HTTP enrichment fetch) is
// deliberately not implemented. This node's only granted authority is
// `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`; it holds no filesystem or HTTP capability.

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        if published.published {
            let mut done: Vec<&str> = Vec::with_capacity(published.considered.len());
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                let key = id.as_str();
                if key.is_empty() || done.contains(&key) {
                    continue;
                }
                done.push(key);
                state_rw::put(key, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

